  "title": "guid-utils: Fix stack-use-after-return",
  "description": "The previous implementation of guids_add_guid used the e_guid_t\nas a key in a wmem_tree with wmem_tree_insert32_array, which\ncopies the key and thus allowed (all) callers to call the function\nwith a pointer to a e_guid_t allocated on the stack.\n\nAfter switching to a wmem_map, the e_guid_t has to be copied to\na key that is heap allocated to avoid using stack allocated memory\nafter it is freed.\n\nOSS Fuzz 485738529\n\nFixup 65d51ec101dfcd8d3b942e2a72b6cea92c9138c1\n\nAI-Assisted: no",
